@startuml
title Owner decision — Never Again — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor Owner
boundary "Browser SPA" as Browser
control "FERTO Worker" as Worker
participant "Spotify Web API" as Spotify
database "D1" as D1

Owner -> Browser: Click "Never" on the current recommendation
Browser -> Worker: POST /api/owner/never-again { trackId }\nOrigin + X-CSRF-Token + owner session cookie

alt Visitor, wrong origin, missing CSRF,\nnot the configured owner, or invalid track id
  Worker --> Browser: 401 / 403 / 400 — before any Spotify call
else Valid owner request
  Worker -> D1: Look up the live recording by Spotify id

  alt v4 row with a confirmed ISRC identity
    Worker -> Worker: Use the isrc: recording key directly
    note right of Worker
      Zero Spotify calls in the common path.
    end note
  else Legacy exact-id row — fallback metadata lookup
    Worker -> Spotify: Grant SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN\n(service token)
    Spotify --> Worker: Access token
    Worker -> Spotify: GET /v1/tracks/{trackId}

    alt 200 with a confirmed ISRC
      Spotify --> Worker: Full track with isrc
      Worker -> Worker: recording_key = isrc:ISRC; retain the\nlegacy spotify:id alias for immediate live removal
    else 200 without an ISRC
      Spotify --> Worker: Track has no usable isrc
      Worker -> Worker: recording_key = spotify:{id}
    else 404 — the track itself is gone
      Spotify --> Worker: Not found
      Worker -> Worker: recording_key = spotify:{id}\n(exact-id exclusion still recorded)
    else Transient failure (5xx, network)
      Spotify --> Worker: Error
      Worker --> Browser: 503 — fail closed
      note right of Worker #FFDDDD
        Fail-closed: an uncertain identity is
        never weakened into a weaker exclusion.
        Nothing is stored and the candidate stays
        visible until the owner can retry.
      end note
    end
  end

  Worker -> D1: INSERT OR IGNORE never_recordings\n(recording_key, isrc, spotify_id) — idempotent
  Worker -> D1: Atomic serialized batch: remove the permanent key\nand any upgraded legacy alias; compact slot ranges + counters
  Worker --> Browser: 200 { ok: true }
  Browser -> Worker: GET /api/recommendation (next track)
  Worker --> Browser: A different recommendation, if one is available
end

note over Worker,D1 #D9EAD3
  Never Again is recording-wide and permanent: every rebuild
  filters the recording key before materializing draw slots,
  so a future rebuild that picks a different
  representative (another pressing, the single edit)
  cannot bring the song back.
end note

@enduml
